# Module Domain Structure

## Target Shape

```text
domain/
  index.ts                      # required — public API
  {module}.domain.module.ts     # required — NestJS @Module
  models/                       # required — business entities (interface)
  types/                        # optional — supporting types / enums
  repositories/                 # optional — @Injectable() persistence classes
  gateways/                     # optional — @Injectable() external API classes
  tools/                        # optional — @Injectable() in-process capabilities
  exceptions/                   # optional — domain errors
  constants.ts                  # optional — module-level constants
```

Minimum: `index.ts` + `{module}.domain.module.ts` + `models/{entity}.ts`.

## Classification Table

| Artifact | Folder | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Business entity | `models/` | `user.ts` → `interface User` |
| Supporting type / enum | `types/` | `user.types.ts` |
| Persistence class | `repositories/` | `user.repository.ts` |
| External API class | `gateways/` | `amo-auth.gateway.ts` |
| In-process capability | `tools/` | `password-hasher.ts` |
| Domain error | `exceptions/` | `user-not-found.ts` → `class UserNotFound` |
| Use case | `src/core/{m}/use-cases/` | `sign-up.case.ts` |
| HTTP controller / filter | `src/http/` | — |
| Prisma model | `src/common/infra/prisma/models/` | `user.prisma` |

## models/

- Business entities as TypeScript `interface` — one per file, kebab-case
  filename, PascalCase interface.
- Do NOT extend Prisma types. Prisma models live in `common/infra/prisma/models/`.
- No DTOs, transport payloads, search params here.

## repositories/ — concrete @Injectable() classes

```ts
import { Injectable } from '@nestjs/common'
import { PrismaService } from '@common/infra/prisma'
import type { New } from '@common/types'
import type { User } from '../models/user'

@Injectable()
export class UserRepository {
  constructor(private readonly prisma: PrismaService) {}

  public async findById(id: number): Promise<User | null> {
    const user = await this.prisma.db.user.findUnique({ where: { id } })
    return user ? this.toDomain(user) : null
  }

  public async create(data: New<User>): Promise<User> {
    const user = await this.prisma.db.user.create({ data })
    return this.toDomain(user)
  }

  public async update(user: User): Promise<User> {
    const { id, ...data } = user
    const updated = await this.prisma.db.user.update({ where: { id }, data })
    return this.toDomain(updated)
  }

  private toDomain(row: User): User { return row }
}
```

- Inject `PrismaService`, access via `this.prisma.db`.
- Accept/return domain models — never expose Prisma types.
- Always have private `toDomain()` mapper.
- Naming: `find*`/`get*` → `T | null`, `list*`/`search*` → `T[]`,
  `create`/`update`/`delete` → standard CRUD.

## exceptions/

- Subclass `DomainException` from `@common/exceptions`.
- File: `{error-name}.ts`, class: `{ErrorName}` — no `Exception` suffix.
- Message: Russian. Code: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`.
- One class per business failure.

```ts
import { DomainException } from '@common/exceptions'

export class UserNotFound extends DomainException {
  constructor(userId: number) {
    super({
      code: 'USER_NOT_FOUND',
      message: `Пользователь с ID ${userId} не найден`,
      metadata: { userId }
    })
  }
}
```

## {module}.domain.module.ts

```ts
@Module({
  providers: [UserRepository, PasswordHasher],
  exports: [UserRepository, PasswordHasher]
})
export class AuthDomainModule {}
```

- Register & export all @Injectable() domain providers.
- NOT re-exported from `domain/index.ts`.

## domain/index.ts — public API

```ts
export type { User } from './models/user'
export { UserNotFound } from './exceptions/user-not-found'
```

- Re-export public surface. Unlisted = internal.
- Domain module NOT re-exported.

## Import Rules

- Neighbor files from same `domain/` — OK.
- `@common/*` — OK.
- Another module's public API via `domain/index.ts` — OK.
- `use-cases/**` from `domain/` — FORBIDDEN (direction: use-cases → domain).
- Barrel paths (`@common/types`), not deep (`@common/types/generics`).

## Anti-Patterns

- External API as `repository` → use `gateway`
- DB as `gateway` → use `repository`
- Interface for single implementation → use class
- Prisma models in `domain/models/` → `common/infra/prisma/models/`
- `any` / `unknown` in method signatures
- Exposing raw DB rows / SDK types from repository/gateway
- Re-exporting domain module from `index.ts`
- Empty folders "for future use"
